<Callout
  title="Experimental"
  subtitle="Carbon has no command palette. CommandPalette follows Carbon's modal, search and list box patterns, and its API may change in a minor release."
/>

## Basic

Pass the commands as `items`, each with a unique id and display text, and bind `open`. Focus moves to the search field when the palette opens and returns to the trigger when it closes. The first match is highlighted, so <DocKbd label="Enter" /> runs it. Arrow keys move the highlight, and <DocKbd label="Escape" /> or a click outside closes the palette.

Listen for `select` to run a command. The palette closes after it; call `event.preventDefault()` to keep it open. The query clears on close.

<FileSource src="/framed/CommandPalette/CommandPalette" />

## Sizes

Set `size` to control the height of the search field and the rows. The default is `"md"`, 40px. `"sm"` is 32px and `"lg"` is 48px.

<FileSource src="/framed/CommandPalette/CommandPaletteSizes" />

## Matching

Typing filters the commands with fuzzy matching and ranks the best matches first: a prefix, then a word start, then a match inside a word, then scattered letters. Matched characters are emphasized. A description matches only when it holds the query as one run, so scattered letters in long text don't pull in unrelated commands. Add `keywords` to match terms that the label does not show. Screen readers hear the number of results as the user types.

Set `highlightMatches` to `false` to drop the emphasis. Pass `match` to change how text is matched; it receives the text and the query and returns whether it matched, an optional score and the indices to emphasize.

## Groups

Set `group` on items to show them under a header. Ungrouped items come first. While the user types, each group moves by its best match. Use the `group` slot to render the header yourself.

<FileSource src="/framed/CommandPalette/CommandPaletteGroups" />

## Keyboard shortcuts

Set `shortcut` on an item to show its key caps, such as `"mod+shift+d"`. `mod` reads <DocKbd label="⌘" /> on macOS and iOS and <DocKbd label="Ctrl" /> elsewhere. The palette shows shortcuts but does not run them.

To open the palette from anywhere, call `onShortcut` in `onMount`. It returns the function that removes the listener, so `onMount` cleans it up. Nothing listens until you call it. A shortcut without a modifier, such as <DocKbd label="/" />, does not fire while the user types in a field. `formatShortcut` returns the key caps for your own labels.

<FileSource src="/framed/CommandPalette/CommandPaletteShortcuts" />

## Links

Set `href` on an item to render it as a link. Selecting it follows the link, and a modifier click opens a new tab. For a client-side router, call `event.preventDefault()` in `select` and navigate yourself.

<FileSource src="/framed/CommandPalette/CommandPaletteLinks" />

## Custom rows

Use the default slot to render a row's content. The slot receives the `item`, whether it is `highlighted`, and the label's `segments`, each with its text and whether it matched.

<FileSource src="/framed/CommandPalette/CommandPaletteCustomRow" />

## Empty state

Set `emptyText` to the message shown when nothing matches, or pass a function to build it from the query. Use the `empty` slot for richer content.

<FileSource src="/framed/CommandPalette/CommandPaletteEmpty" />

## Footer

Use the `footer` slot for hints or secondary actions under the results.

<FileSource src="/framed/CommandPalette/CommandPaletteFooter" />

## Layering

The palette starts a [Layer](/components/Layer) wherever it renders, like a modal, so it looks the same when it opens from a layered surface.

<FileSource src="/framed/CommandPalette/CommandPaletteLayer" />

## Width

The palette is 640px wide, or the window width on small screens. Set the `--ccs-command-palette-width` custom property to change it, for all palettes with `:root { --ccs-command-palette-width: 48rem; }` or for one with `<CommandPalette --ccs-command-palette-width="48rem">`.

## Right-to-left

Inside a `dir="rtl"` page or a [LayoutDirection](/components/LayoutDirection), the icons, the highlight bar and the key caps move to the other side. To render the palette outside a transformed container, wrap it in a [Portal](/components/Portal), which keeps the direction and the [ThemeZone](/components/ThemeZone) theme.

<FileSource src="/framed/CommandPalette/CommandPaletteRtl" />

## Async results

For results from a server, set `shouldFilter` to `false` and update `items` on `search`. Set `debounce` to wait for a pause in typing before `search` fires, and set `loading` while the request runs.

<FileSource src="/framed/CommandPalette/CommandPaletteAsync" />

## Large lists

Above 100 items, the palette renders only the rows in view. Set `virtualize` to `false` to render every row, or pass an object to tune it, as in [ComboBox](/components/ComboBox#virtualization).

<FileSource src="/framed/CommandPalette/CommandPaletteVirtualized" />
